From: Herrie <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 16:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3566-pinetab2: let the WiFi chip wake the host

Two things stopped the BES2600 from ever waking the board.

The rail was switched off. vcc_wl is the vmmc-supply for &sdmmc1, and it
carried regulator-state-mem { regulator-off-in-suspend; } while the same
&sdmmc1 node asks for keep-power-in-suspend and cap-sdio-irq. Those
contradict each other, and the regulator wins: the chip loses its 3.3 V
in suspend, so no WoWLAN filter it has been given can match anything and
WIFI_WAKE_HOST_H can never be asserted. Drop the override so the rail
follows the node's keep-power-in-suspend.

The node was not wakeup-capable. It already names the line both ways --
interrupts = <RK_PC4 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING> and host-wakeup-gpios -- and
the driver now resolves that into an IRQ and arms it with
enable_irq_wake() for the duration of a suspend. device_set_wakeup_enable()
only works on a device the firmware description marks as a wake source,
so add wakeup-source.

Neither of these is enough on its own, and neither is sufficient without
the matching driver change (bes2600_wlan_bt_hostwake_register, which was
a stub that logged "this function does nothing").

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific WiFi bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Herrie <claude.ai@herrie.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts
@@ -20,10 +20,11 @@
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		vin-supply = <&vcc3v3_sys>;
-
-		regulator-state-mem {
-			regulator-off-in-suspend;
-		};
+		/*
+		 * No regulator-state-mem/regulator-off-in-suspend here: this is
+		 * the vmmc-supply for &sdmmc1, which asks for
+		 * keep-power-in-suspend so the chip can wake the host.
+		 */
 	};
 
 	sdio_pwrseq: sdio-pwrseq {
@@ -124,6 +125,7 @@
 		pinctrl-0 = <&host_wake_wl &wifi_wake_host_h &wifi_regon>;
 
 		interrupt-parent = <&gpio0>;
+		wakeup-source;
 		interrupts = <RK_PC4 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 
 		/*
